course: dictionary
lesson: 11161
title: Windfall
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A windfall is a word with two meanings, and the clues around it tell you which one you need. Money is the first meaning. «A windfall is money you did not expect, like a gift from Gran.» The clue is did not expect: this money arrives by surprise, with no plan behind it.
explain: The second meaning is about trees. Sometimes the wind blows apples off a tree and they land on the grass. These fallen apples are windfalls too. If a sentence talks about a tree, an orchard or a garden, think of fruit, not money.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense. «We picked up windfalls under the apple tree» makes sense with fruit. «An unexpected windfall paid for our trip» makes sense with money.
fact: Windfall means money or a gift that you did not expect.
fact: «A windfall is money you did not expect, like a gift from Gran.»
fact: A windfall can also be a fruit, especially an apple, blown off a tree by the wind.
fact: Useful phrases are "a windfall of" and "an unexpected windfall".
fact: Sensible people may save part of a windfall, so it does not all disappear quickly.
exercise: «A windfall is money you did not expect, like a gift from Gran.» What is a windfall in this sentence? | *Money you did not expect | A tree that has been blown over | A long walk in the park | A type of wet weather
exercise: After the storm, we picked up windfalls under the apple tree. What are the windfalls? | *Apples blown off the tree by the wind | Birds that sing at night | Money found in the grass | Branches of the tree
exercise: Mum said, "We got an unexpected windfall!" What does she mean? | We were sad and tired | *We had a lucky gain we did not plan | We lost our keys | We had a big meal at home
test: Ravi put part of his windfall in a jar to save. What does windfall mean here? | A heavy rainstorm | *Money he did not expect | A tree in the garden | A sad song
test: The windfall lay in the grass, bruised from its fall from the tree. What does windfall mean here? | A gift of money | *A fruit blown off the tree by the wind | A kind of bird | A grey, wet day
exam: Which sentence uses windfall to mean money? | The windfall was red and sweet | The windfall tree was very tall | We picked up windfalls in the orchard | *A windfall of prize money arrived in the post
